# Optional. Set this as a plain server env var in your Vercel project
# settings (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables) -- no VITE_
# prefix. api/gemini.js reads it fresh on every cold start, so you don't
# need to rebuild the Vite app for a change to take effect -- redeploying
# (even a no-op redeploy) is enough to pick up a new/changed value.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT use VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY for this. Any VITE_-prefixed
# var gets inlined into the public JS bundle by Vite, which would expose
# the real key to anyone who opens dev tools on the live site -- this repo
# used to do exactly that and it was a real, fixed security issue. The
# frontend now calls /api/gemini (a serverless function) instead of
# Google directly, and that function is the only thing that ever reads
# this key.
#
# Gemini API key for LIVE AI lead generation (Gemini 2.5 Flash + Google Search
# grounding). Get one free at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Without it, the app still works keyless: the welcome screen, free Sample
# Campaign, campaign manager, CSV export, payment verification flow, and
# session-recovery scan all run client-side. Live lead generation shows a
# clear message explaining the key is missing instead of failing cryptically.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
